  "weekly_note": "This week featured several lopsided wins driven by large single-player outliers (e.g., Jahmyr Gibbs, Dak/DJ Moore), multiple defenses exceeding projections (Falcons, Packers, Rams, Browns), and several managers holding high-scoring bench players (Hunter Henry, Emanuel Wilson, Chimere Dike, Christian Kirk) who could have swung close matchups. Injuries/inactives and BYEs (notable: Aaron Rodgers, Kyler Murray, Tyreek Hill, several teams with BYE-impacted players) had visible impact on outcomes. Several close games were decided by kicker/defense performances and bench decisions." 
